---
/**
 * Privacy, the concrete promises of a static, no-backend site.
 */
import ArticleLayout from '../shared/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { websiteJsonLd } from '../shared/seo/jsonld';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Satvik.fyi privacy promise: no trackers, no cookies, no accounts, no personal data. Local storage only, on your device."
  path="/privacy/"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  jsonLd={[websiteJsonLd(SITE)]}
>
  <p>
    This site is built to make a short privacy policy possible. It is a collection of static pages:
    there is no login, no database, no server-side code processing your requests, and nothing that
    can identify you.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No advertising or ad trackers of any kind.</li>
    <li>No analytics cookies, and no other cookies.</li>
    <li>No accounts, newsletter sign-up forms, or contact forms on this domain.</li>
    <li>No collection of personal data, not your name, email, or location.</li>
    <li>No selling or sharing of data, because there is no data to sell.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Local storage (on your device only)</h2>
  <p>
    Interactive conveniences, beginning with the weekly meal planner, later the dosha quiz; save
    your preferences in your browser’s <em>local storage</em> under versioned
    <code>satvikfyi:…</code> keys. That data never leaves your device, is never transmitted to us,
    and is removed when you clear your browser storage.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages embed YouTube videos using YouTube’s privacy-enhanced
    (<code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>) mode, which sets no tracking cookies until you play the
    video. Once you press play, YouTube’s own policies apply. When the newsletter, shop or community
    spaces launch, they will live on external services reached via clearly labelled subdomains, and
    their policies will be stated on those services, not here.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Our hosting provider may keep short-lived, standard
    technical request logs (as any web server does) for security and abuse prevention; we do not
    receive or use them. If privacy-friendly, aggregate-only analytics are ever added, this page
    will say so plainly before they are switched on.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
